   "line": [
    "Qa5"
   ],
   "spoken": "The lasting point of the whole exchange is that the opponent's central pawn is badly weakened, left leaning on a single defending bishop — and it's never healthy to have a piece chained to a pawn. Meanwhile a knight is already routing toward c5, where it will pile onto that very pawn.",
